        "original_id": "2357ce88-8bd7-55bc-a87f-00ebd3a9e618",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Cornell, Sully Erna, Tony Rombola, Robbie Merrill, Shannon Larkin\n- Bands: Godsmack\n- Songs: \"Burden in My Hand\", \"Releasing the Demons\"\n- Albums: Down on the Upside, Faceless\n- Places: Lawrence, Massachusetts\n\nFacts:\n- Chris Cornell was born Christopher John Boyle on July 20, 1964, and he was an American musician, singer, and songwriter.\n- Godsmack is an American rock band from Lawrence, Massachusetts, formed in 1995.\n- \"Burden in My Hand\" was written by Chris Cornell and was released on September 18, 1996, as the second single from the 1996 album Down on the Upside.\n- Godsmack is composed of founder, frontman, and songwriter Sully Erna, guitarist Tony Rombola, bassist Robbie Merrill, and drummer Shannon Larkin.\n- \"Releasing the Demons\" is a song by Godsmack from the band's third studio album Faceless, and it was written by Sully Erna.\n- Chris Cornell died on May 18, 2017.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
